Allbirds replaces petroleum synthetics with natural alternatives: sugarcane, wool, tree fiber, and organic cotton. The company committed to halving per-product carbon footprint by end-2025 and achieving near-zero by 2030. In 2022, Allbirds reduced carbon by 19% through renewable materials and supply chain logistics optimization. The flagship Moonshot shoe achieves ~1kg CO2 footprint—offset-free carbon neutral. Allbirds bans unsold inventory disposal and partners with Soles4Souls for upcycling returns. The Remix collection repurposes landfill-bound waste into footwear using 99% less water and 65% fewer emissions than traditional production. By prioritizing material innovation, transparency, and closed-loop product recovery, Allbirds demonstrates how sustainable sourcing and thoughtful material selection reduce environmental burden across product lifecycles.